{
  "_comment": "A market map of the robotics, robot-model and robot-data space, written by hand. The derived watch lists can only find publishers already in the index, which is why they missed TheRobotStudio (SO-ARM100, 6,800 stars, the arm behind 64 of our datasets), unitreerobotics (unitree_sdk2, 1,200 stars) and Pantheon (Argus, published two days before a harvest). This list exists to be independent of what we have already seen.",
  "_scope": "Includes companies that publish no hardware at all: foundation-model labs, data-tooling companies, simulation vendors and big-tech research groups. A company earns a place by mattering to the field, not by selling a robot. Several entries publish nothing at all — Figure and Tesla among them — and are listed so that the absence is a recorded fact rather than an oversight.",
  "_handles": "github and huggingface are account handles. verified:true means the handle has been confirmed to exist; verified:false means it is a best guess. A wrong handle costs one wasted API call and returns nothing, so the cost of guessing is far lower than the cost of omitting. Anything marked false should be confirmed before the list is relied on.",
  "_updated": "2026-10-07",
